WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.088
Five workstreams carry the work: identity,
policy, services, compute and access.

2
00:00:06.088 --> 00:00:08.804
They run together, because
finishing one before

3
00:00:08.804 --> 00:00:11.421
starting the next roughly
doubles the program.

4
00:00:11.421 --> 00:00:12.717
They still have an order.

5
00:00:12.717 --> 00:00:16.033
Identity comes first,
because policy, access,

6
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:20.352
devices and data all decide
based on who or what is asking.

7
00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:22.089
Policy follows identity.

8
00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:25.809
Services, naming and
addressing, can run in parallel.

9
00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:29.091
Compute comes mid to late,
and access comes later,

10
00:00:29.091 --> 00:00:32.176
because it consumes both
identity and policy.

11
00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:36.367
The master plan organized the same
work as five technology pillars,

12
00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:39.839
and that left two gaps: nobody
owned the question of which

13
00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:43.533
policy surface owns a setting,
and access had no pillar at all.

14
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:47.373
Book 01 closes them, with a
security-engineering lead for

15
00:00:47.373 --> 00:00:51.312
policy and a joint identity
and security lead for access.

16
00:00:51.312 --> 00:00:56.478
Every week lost in assessment or
attribute design moves every later gate,

17
00:00:56.478 --> 00:01:00.468
and one dependency never
relaxes: PKI waits for identity.

18
00:01:00.468 --> 00:01:06.173
The decision, during Phase 0: name the five
workstream leads, including those two.

19
00:01:06.173 --> 00:01:07.476
Next, the projects.
